KG42.register("rules-2a1708fe00bd88ccd1b7097f",{"id":"23-hierarchical_market_structure::v141-c-R003","paper":"23-hierarchical_market_structure","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R003","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","name":"Consumer participation","process_stage":"participation","market_meaning":"A microgrid may serve its local demand economically from the distribution network under the described total-generation-capacity bidding policy. Scope: DNEM; microgrids choosing the described policy of bidding total generation capacity and serving local demand from the distribution network.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function participation.consumer under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["participation.consumer"],"E":[],"omega":{"market_type":"DEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"participation","context_text":"DNEM; microgrids choosing the described policy of bidding total generation capacity and serving local demand from the distribution network.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E008"]},"x":[],"theta":[],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R003-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"A microgrid may serve its local demand economically from the distribution network under the described total-generation-capacity bidding policy. Scope: DNEM; microgrids choosing the described policy of bidding total generation capacity and serving local demand from the distribution network.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["participation.consumer"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E008"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E008","location":{"location_id":"src-fbc18f73e3-p03-c2r3__v141-a-M01-bidding","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":"II-B Microgrids Objective","anchor_text":"ds ψ′ ≤ψ′j ≤ψ′j (2) jme- he ρ′j = ψ′j 2αjPje + βj ; Pje = Pj. (3) nd e on B. Microgrids Objective de","equation_id":"(4)-(6)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Microgrid m maximizes the payoff function (4), subjected to the limitations on the bidding vector as shown in (5). Here, the first term in the payoff function is the revenue of the microgrid and the second term is the generation cost. The generation dispatch of microgrids is provided by curtailing the IL and dispatching the DERs. The microgrid may adopt several policies to serve its demand. One policy is to serve local demand and bid the excess generation in the DNEM while the other is to bid on its total generation capacity in the DNEM and serve the local demand economically from the distribution network. In both cases, the bidding vector for generation in microgrid m is shown in (6)\nR_m = \\max_{P_m,\\psi_m} \\left[ \\lambda_0 \\cdot P_m - \\left(\\alpha_m P_m^2 + \\beta_m P_m + \\gamma_m\\right) \\right] \\tag{4}\n\\underline{\\psi}_m \\le \\psi_m \\le \\bar{\\psi}_m \\tag{5}\n\\rho_m = \\psi_m(2\\alpha_m P_{me} + \\beta_m); \\quad \\sum_e P_{me} = P_m. \\tag{6}"}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":"C explicitly supplied only source-backed unary facts for this function; other graph gaps remain reviewable.","empty_x_reason":"No design-selection or operational variable is defined for the scoped policy choice or for microgrid local demand in the supplied source. The microgrid dispatch P_m and bidding strategy psi_m appearing in equations (4)-(6) are used by the bidding/clearing formulation, not by this participation-consumer statement.","empty_theta_reason":"No fixed input or constant is defined for the scoped policy choice or for serving local demand from the distribution network. The cost coefficients alpha_m, beta_m, gamma_m and price lambda_0 in equations (4)-(6) parameterize the microgrid payoff/bidding formulation, not this participation statement."},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M01-bidding","v141-a-M01-participation"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"participation.consumer","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E008","quote":"The microgrid may adopt several policies to serve its demand. One policy is to serve local demand and bid the excess generation in the DNEM while the other is to bid on its total generation capacity in the DNEM and serve the local demand economically from the distribution network."}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"7f414139e009fdaba130ffa8ed0bf3a611c280c6c14802eea530b10494602597","applicability":"non_mathematical","reason":"The cited source states this as a qualitative participation policy: 'One policy is to serve local demand and bid the excess generation in the DNEM while the other is to bid on its total generation capacity in the DNEM and serve the local demand economically from the distribution network.' It does not define a policy-choice variable, a microgrid local-demand variable, or a participation constraint for serving local demand from the distribution network. The nearby equations (4)-(6) formulate the microgrid payoff and generation-bidding vector and are not a constraint specific to consumer participation; those equations belong to the bidding/clearing rules. The scoped rule is therefore procedural rather than a failed mathematical extraction.","bindings":[{"object_id":"v141-c-R003-C001","node_ids":["participation.consumer"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"C001 is the sole procedural participation statement and is owned by participation.consumer. The frozen graph contains no edges for this rule, so no edge is bound."}],"revision_requests":[]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
